5. Adding and verifying contacts
   ID: doc_everyone_pay_everyone_pay_004
   Score: 9.6609
   Content: ## Add contacts
- Go to Everyone Pay and select Add Contact.
- Enter a username, email, or mobile number and confirm the contact’s display details.
- You can save up to $550 contacts, so consider adding frequent recipients for faster checkout.

## Verify contacts
- Contact verification before the first transaction: Yes.
- To verify a contact, open their profile and follow the prompts to confirm identity details.
- Verified contacts display a clear indicator so you can send with greater confidence.

## Managing your contact list
- Edit a contact to update names, labels, or notes.
- Remove contacts you no longer use to keep your list organized.
- Use search and filters to quickly locate a contact when sending.

6. Joint Business Holders: Adding Multiple Account Owners
   ID: doc_business_savings_accounts_joint_business_holders_+_user_roles_001
   Score: 8.9926
   Content: ## Eligibility and limits
You can add joint business account owners up to a maximum of 4.

## How to add a new owner
- Gather required details for the prospective owner, including legal name, contact information, tax identification, and role within the business.
- From your account dashboard, open the ownership or account access section and choose Add owner.
- Enter the owner’s details exactly as they appear on official records, then submit for review.
- Complete identity verification and any business authorization steps requested during submission.
- Review the ownership agreement and any updates to account responsibilities, then confirm the addition.

## Assigning roles during the addition process
- If you plan to assign Admin, Finance, or Auditor access to a new owner at the time of addition, you can apply those permissions as part of the same request.
- The one-time fee for setting up advanced user roles and permissions is $0.00.

## After submission
- Each added owner will receive an invitation to accept ownership and complete any remaining verification tasks.
- You can monitor the status of each invite and resend or cancel invitations if needed.
- Once accepted and verified, the new owner will appear in your ownership list and, if assigned, their user role will be active.

## Tips for smooth processing
- Ensure the business name and registration details match exactly across all documents.
- Use a consistent business email domain for ownership invitations to help with recognition and delivery.
- Confirm that every owner understands their responsibilities and any dual-approval rules that may apply to high-impact actions.

7. Gold Plus Saver Account: Mobile banking and deposit limits
   ID: doc_business_savings_accounts_gold_plus_saver_005
   Score: 8.7612
   Content: ## Mobile check deposit
- Your daily mobile deposit limit is $15,000. Deposits above this amount are not accepted via mobile on the same day.
- Endorse checks clearly and use well-lit images to reduce rejections.
- If you approach $15,000, consider depositing remaining items on a later day or using an alternative deposit method.

### Best practices for mobile deposits
- Verify payee, amount, and endorsement before submission.
- Retain the physical check until it clears in your account.

## Outbound transfer limits
- The maximum daily transfer amount from this account is $50,000.
- This cap applies across supported transfer methods initiated from this savings account.

### Managing daily caps
- Batch payments to stay within $50,000.
- For transactions exceeding $50,000, split transfers over multiple days or choose another permitted method consistent with policy.

### Visibility and controls
- Review your daily totals before initiating new payments to avoid surpassing $50,000.
- Use approval workflows to ensure large movements are planned within available headroom.

8. Earning rewards for good grades
   ID: doc_checking_accounts_dark_green_account_004
   Score: 8.7381
   Content: ## What you can earn

- Annual cash bonus: You receive $62.50 each year you verify a 3.0+ GPA.
- Savings APY boosts when you qualify:
  - Linked Bronze Savings Account: 0.85% APY boost
  - Linked Platinum Plus Savings Account: 0.45% APY boost
- The boost is added to the standard APY of the eligible linked savings account(s) and applies only while your good‑standing status is active.

## Eligibility criteria

You qualify for rewards when:
- Your most recently completed academic year (or cumulative) GPA is 3.0 or higher on a 4.0 scale.
- You are the Dark Green Account holder whose name appears on the transcript/verification.
- Your documentation clearly shows your full name, institution, term(s) covered, and GPA.

Notes:
- If your school does not use a 4.0 scale, provide the school’s official scale or conversion so we can confirm the 3.0+ equivalent.
- Part‑time, transfer, and graduate students are eligible as long as GPA can be verified.

## How to verify your GPA

1. Obtain proof of your GPA from your registrar or student portal.
2. Submit your documentation through the Rho-Bank app or secure message center.
3. Ensure your submission includes:
   - Full name matching your account
   - Institution name
   - Term(s) or academic year covered
   - Cumulative or academic‑year GPA
   - Grading scale if not on a 4.0 scale

Accepted documents:
- Official or unofficial transcript (PDF or clear image)
- Registrar letter on school letterhead stating GPA and term(s)
- Third‑party enrollment/GPA verification service results that include your GPA and school source

Tips:
- Combine multiple pages into a single file if needed.
- If you transferred schools, include transcripts from each institution covering the relevant period.

## When rewards are applied

- Review and approval: We typically confirm eligibility shortly after you submit complete documentation.
- Cash bonus: $62.50 is deposited once per 12‑month verification period after approval.
- APY boosts: If you have a linked savings account, the boost begins shortly after approval and remains active for up to 12 months or until your eligibility period ends, whichever comes first.

## Maintaining and renewing your rewards

- Annual re‑verification is required. Submit updated GPA proof each year to continue receiving $62.50 and any applicable APY boosts.
- If your GPA falls below 3.0 for a period, you will not receive the bonus for that verification cycle, and APY boosts will end when the previously verified period expires. You can re‑qualify by submitting new proof once your GPA meets the threshold again.
- If you change or unlink a savings account, any active APY boost applies only to eligible linked accounts going forward.

## Common scenarios

- Pass/Fail or alternative grading: Include the school’s explanation of how performance maps to a 4.0 scale (or an official conversion).
- Quarter vs. semester systems: Provide the transcript summarizing the full academic year or cumulative GPA.
- Transfers: If your GPA resets at the new school, submit the most recent cumulative GPA available; include prior school records if needed to confirm a full academic year at or above 3.0.
- Study abroad: Provide the host or home institution’s transcript showing GPA or the official conversion.
- Graduation mid‑year: Submit your final transcript; you remain eligible for the final verification period if the GPA requirement is met.

## If your submission is declined

Common reasons:
- Missing GPA or grading scale
- Name on the document does not match your account
- Unreadable or incomplete files
- GPA reported is below 3.0

How to fix it:
- Re‑submit a clear, complete document with the required details
- Add the school’s official grading scale or conversion if not on a 4.0 system
- Ensure the name and institution match exactly

Once corrected and approved, your $62.50 and any applicable 0.85% or 0.45% APY boost will be applied for the current verification period.

9. Why can't I send money to this contact?
   ID: doc_everyone_pay_everyone_pay_011
   Score: 8.2269
   Content: ## Common reasons
- The contact has not been verified and your account requires verification before the first transaction: Yes.
- You have blocked this user or they have blocked you.
- The contact information is invalid or no longer active.
- The recipient’s account cannot receive payments at this time.
- A security review is temporarily restricting the transfer.

## What you can do
- Open the contact card and complete verification if required.
- Confirm the contact’s username, email, or mobile number via a trusted channel.
- Check your block list and unblock the user if appropriate.
- Try again later if you see a temporary restriction message.
- If the issue persists, contact support from the failed transaction details.

10. Joint Business Holders: Legal Requirements and Documentation
   ID: doc_business_savings_accounts_joint_business_holders_+_user_roles_005
   Score: 8.0985
   Content: ## Ownership structure and limits
- You may designate up to 4 joint business account holders.
- Ensure your corporate governance documents authorize multiple holders and reflect current officers or managers.

## Required documentation
- Formation and registration documents that establish legal existence and authority to bank.
- A resolution or comparable authorization naming the individuals who may act on behalf of the business.
- Identity verification materials for each holder, along with any required beneficial ownership information.
- Tax identification and business contact details that match state or country records.

## Dual authorization considerations
- The dual-authorization control Yes applies to certain transactions and high-impact account actions.
- When this control is in effect, specified actions must be approved by separate authorized users before completion.
- Document your internal approval policy and ensure all holders acknowledge the required review and approval flow.

## Submission guidance
- Provide consistent legal names across all documents and avoid abbreviations that do not appear in official records.
- Maintain current governance documents to prevent delays when adding or updating holders.
- Retain copies of resolutions and authorization evidence for audits and compliance reviews.


