2. Virtual Card Management: Creating One-Time Use Cards for Security
   ID: doc_credit_cards_virtual_card_management_005
   Score: 12.9139
   Content: ## Availability
- One-time (single-use) virtual cards must be enabled: Yes

## Create a one-time use card
1. Go to Cards > Virtual and select Create new card.
2. Choose the one-time use option (availability: Yes).
3. Confirm and generate the card details.
4. Use the card for a single transaction and do not store it for future use.

## Usage notes
- After one successful authorization, the card is no longer usable for additional payments.
- If a transaction fails, you may need to generate a new one-time card and retry.
- Share the card details only with the intended payee and avoid saving them in vendor profiles.

3. Platinum Rewards Card: Using Virtual Cards for Online Shopping and Subscriptions
   ID: doc_credit_cards_platinum_rewards_card_006
   Score: 11.1248
   Content: ## When to Use Virtual Cards
- Online checkouts with unfamiliar merchants to reduce exposure of your primary card number.
- Recurring subscriptions so you can pause or delete a specific merchant without affecting other services.
- One-time purchases where you prefer a card number you can retire after use.

## Capacity and Access
- Virtual cards are included with your membership: Yes.
- Maintain up to 30 active virtual cards at once to organize spend by merchant or purpose.

## Practical Tips
- Assign clear nicknames to match the website or app where the card is used.
- Set per-card limits aligned to expected monthly subscription amounts.
- If a merchant is compromised, delete that virtual card and create a new one without replacing your physical card.

## Cost
- There is no additional fee for using virtual cards beyond the standard annual fee of $200.00.

4. Virtual Card Management: Creating Instant Virtual Cards for Your Team
   ID: doc_business_credit_cards_virtual_card_management_001
   Score: 10.7349
   Content: ## Before you start
- Confirm capacity: you can maintain up to $275 active virtual cards at once.
- Organize your structure: create up to 30 team groups to align cards with departments or projects.

## Create an instant virtual card
1. Go to the Virtual Cards page and select **Create Virtual Card**.
2. Choose the **Team/Department** to associate the card with (or create a new team group if needed).
3. Enter the **card nickname**, set any initial card parameters (e.g., purpose, spending scope), and assign a card owner.
4. Select **Issue**. The card is ready to use within 5 seconds.

### What happens after issuance
- The new card appears in your team’s card list immediately after the 5-second provisioning completes.
- Share the card details with authorized team members using your organization’s secure communication practices.

## Assigning cards across teams
- Use consistent naming conventions so each card clearly maps to its team.
- Balance card counts across departments to stay within the $275 limit.
- If you are scaling quickly, plan your card allocation per department in advance, keeping the limit of 30 groups in mind.

## Tips for smooth onboarding
- Pre-create team groups so admins can issue cards without delay.
- Maintain an internal request workflow so team leads can request and receive virtual cards within 5 seconds when needed.

5. Virtual Card Management: Getting Started with Virtual Cards
   ID: doc_credit_cards_virtual_card_management_001
   Score: 10.5622
   Content: ## Quick setup checklist
- Confirm instant issuance availability: Yes
- Expected issuance time: 5 seconds
- Maximum active virtual cards per account: 60
